en:
{{collapse list|Can be done very easily as the {{flag|USA|United States}}, who start with a strong Rural Folk and {{law|No Migration Controls|text=link}}.|
* First, invite Juan Lavalle and have him assume leadership of the {{icon|Landowners}} Southern Planters. Wait for the 1836 election to finish, while attempting to make the southern planters win the election. Juan Lavalle should then become president, due to the Southern Planters having more clout than the {{icon|Rural folk}} Yeoman Farmers. After that, use the Yeoman Farmers to pass {{law|Closed Borders|text=link}}.}}

- id=\"Vox Populi\"

Note that Getulio Vargas is not actually required—this can be completed earlier than 1909 with completion of the New Republic journal entry.
{{icon|cotsb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Federation Day\"

{{collapse list|During the [[Italy#Scripted_content|''Risorgimento'']] journal entry, by having enough radicals in your country, an event ''Tricolors Over [Capital City]'' will fire and force the democratic system upon you, allowing for you to skip the process of slow reforms entirely.|
* However, if the number of radicals isn't reduced, it can cause you to be annexed by another Italian country. Also, note that you do not need to ''start'' the game as the Papal States, only be the Papal States at some point before forming Italy. The ''Risorgimento'' mechanics allow any Italian nation to be annexed by another Italian nation with the player switching to the annexing nation. Thus, it is possible (though unlikely) that you can switch to play as the Papal States after going through the Italian powers, and thereby have enough states to form Italy.}}

- id=\"Stonks\"

The technology {{technology|Empiricism}} is required to implement {{law|State Atheism}}. No IG will support the law by default, and the {{icon|Intelligentsia|3=1}} will only support it if the player is currently on {{law|State Religion}}, so a {{ideology|Communist}}, {{ideology|Positivist}} or {{ideology|Nihilist}} IG leader or movement is recommended. If getting countries to join an atheist Ideological Union proves difficult, releasing countries as [[subjects]] will do the job.<br>Best paired with the 'Euphoric' achievement.
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

- id=\"Declaration of Independence\"

Forming {{flag|Turkestan}} or {{flag|Pakistan}} blocks the achievement.
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

- id=\"For Twelve Years You Have Been Asking\"

The final goal is asymmetrical with {{flag|Russia}} and {{flag|Great Britain}} having different goals from the central Asian countries. The two great powers have the easiest goals.
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

- id=\"Iranzamin\"

80% literacy is only needed in the incorporated states. Start by building a university in every incorporated state and promote social mobility in as many of them as possible, starting with the most populated. The countries to the east is easily conquered and will bolster your armies, but leave a strip of land between you and India as a buffer. Once these are captured and you've colonized as much of the north as possible, keep switching alliances with Britain and Russia to secure the remaining territory. Literacy will hit 80% by 1890 this way. It is advisable to ''not'' incorporate some of the later conquests, as their literacy rate will take a long time to catch up.
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

- id=\"Hermit Kingdom\"

{{Collapse list|The ''Gyojo Shinwon'' journal entry is activated by an pulse event of the ''The Donghak Movement'' journal entry, which requires the following:|
** 1. Research {{technology|Human Rights|text=link}}
** 2. Do not have {{law|Isolationism|text=link}} enacted
** 3. Any [[power bloc]] lead by a European country has more than 0 {{iconify|leverage|power bloc}} advantage over Korea.
** 4. {{red|10%}} or more of Korea's pops are {{icon|radical|3=1}}
''The Donghak Movement'' journal entry ends 'early' when either {{red|5%}} or less of Korea's pops are {{icon|radical|3=1}} or the {{icon|Rural Folk|3=1}} are supporting a revolutionary [[political movement]].

Then, there is a 1 in 11 chance each month of triggering the event ''The Samrye Petition'' which requires {{red|20%}} or more of Korea's pops are {{icon|radical|3=1}} and that the {{icon|Rural Folk|3=1}} are in opposition and not marginalized. Select the second option to start the ''Gyojo Shinwon'' journal entry. ''Gyojo Shinwon'' requires the following to complete:
** 1. Enact {{law|Isolationism|text=link}}
** 2. Do not have {{law|State Religion|text=link}} enacted
** 3. The {{icon|Landowners|3=1}} are in opposition and not powerful
This journal entry also fails if the {{icon|Rural Folk|3=1}} are supporting a revolutionary [[political movement]], and otherwise times out after 10 years.}}
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

- id=\"Honor and Life\"

{{collapse list|Becoming a protectorate of Great Britain makes it much easier to fight off Russia.|
* Reload until Great Britain’s attitude towards you is \"domineering\". Declare a interest in England and launch a diplomatic play against Britain, then it should set \"making you a protectorate\" as primary demand. Just back down to become protectorate of Britain.
* With Great Britain’s protection, you can keep Russia from invading you for quite a long time. Since Circassia has access to the sea, you can expand yourself by colonization or conquering.
* A random event will add North Caucasian as a primary culture, which has Mideast heritage. With that, you can simply conquer every Mideast country to strengthen yourself. When prepared, attack the Russians to get state of Kuban to trigger the achievement. (You can see before declaring war if the British are likely to join you.)}}
{{icon|soib|w=36px}}

